    {
      "id": "p0026-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Despite their differences, DVDs, Blu-rays, and VHS tapes can all hold the same movie. These formats aren't compatible with each other, though - you can't just stick a VHS tape into a DVD player. Languages are very similar - they can say roughly the same things, but you can't just shove text from one language into another and hope it'll work right.",
        "raw": "Despite their differences, DVDs, Blu-rays, and VHS tapes can all hold the same\nmovie. These formats aren't compatible with each other, though - you can't\njust stick a VHS tape into a DVD player. Languages are very similar - they can\nsay roughly the same things, but you can't just shove text from one language\ninto another and hope it'll work right.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28741574,
          0.08888571,
          0.89004764,
          0.17419286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28539609,
          0.08817143,
          0.89895428,
          0.17526429
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "DVD、蓝光和 VHS 录像带虽各不相同，却都能装下同一部电影。不过，它们彼此并不兼容：你不能把 VHS 录像带塞进 DVD 播放器。语言也很相似，能表达大致相同的内容，却不能把一种语言的文字硬塞进另一种，就指望一切正常。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
