    {
      "id": "p0026-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Not every language uses punctuation the same way. Some languages have similar-looking punctuation marks that serve different purposes. And some languages have punctuation marks that don't exist in other languages. Because of this, a literal translation with all of the original punctuation intact can have unintended effects.",
        "raw": "Not every language uses punctuation the same way. Some languages have\nsimilar-looking punctuation marks that serve different purposes. And some\nlanguages have punctuation marks that don't exist in other languages. Because\nof this, a literal translation with all of the original punctuation intact can have\nunintended effects.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28901126,
          0.40985714,
          0.89018902,
          0.49683571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28539609,
          0.40914286,
          0.89895428,
          0.49790714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          19,
          21,
          23,
          25,
          27
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "不是所有语言都以同样方式使用标点。有些标点看起来相似，用途却不同；有些标点在其他语言里根本不存在。因此，直译时照搬原来的全部标点，可能产生意料之外的效果。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
